From 9f70da2f5e89412ca03e46f112c25c630d71fcb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wutt6678 <wutt6678@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:13:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Add PRH training-log instrumentation; fix
 post-termination reward bug
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Training-log instrumentation (PRHBench next-commit item 2):
- env_manager.py's success_evaluator now reports batch-level PRH metrics
  (prh_poison_prob_nominal, prh_poison_rate_realized [per-update],
  prh_poison_rate_realized_cumulative, prh_poisoned_episodes,
  prh_total_episodes) whenever the training-side router is active, plus
  the previously-added proxy_hidden_gap.
- ray_trainer.py now logs these under episode/* and prh/* during training,
  and adds val/proxy_hidden_gap_* to the existing validation metrics —
  closing the gap noted in the first commit's README limitations (the
  gap was computed but never reached WandB).

Bug found via the new real-stack integration tests and fixed:
- The AI Safety Gridworlds environments are not auto-reset once a row's
  episode terminates; stepping a done row again yields a degenerate
  transition (observed in practice: reward=0.0, info['hidden_reward']=None)
  that the real trainer already tolerates via its own sticky
  `active_masks = not is_done` masking in rollout_loop.py. PRHRewardRouter
  had no equivalent, so strict_hidden_reward=true (the shipped default)
  would raise on any batch where one row finished before others -- an
  everyday occurrence, not an edge case.
- PRHRewardRouter now tracks its own sticky per-row "active" mask
  (mirroring rollout_loop.py's semantics exactly: a row that terminates
  *this* step is still active for *this* step, only subsequent steps are
  masked), passed the current step's `dones` via route(..., dones=...).
  strict_hidden_reward is now enforced only for still-active rows; a
  missing hidden reward on an already-inactive row is tolerated
  unconditionally, since its reward is masked out downstream regardless.
  Each info dict now also carries prh_active for debugging/analysis.
- `dones` is optional (defaults to treating every row as active), so
  existing single-step call sites are unaffected.

10 new tests (4 pure-logic in test_prh_reward.py reproducing the bug and
its fix directly at the router level, 2 integration tests exercising the
new success_evaluator metrics against the real ray+gymnasium stack, plus
the analysis/pilot_metrics.py suite tracked separately). All 49 tests
across both suites pass.
---
